Description: CVE-2026-63385 - http: Reject headers containing CRLF
 Reject HTTP header values that contain a carriage return or line feed.
 The previous implementation accepted deprecated obs-fold (RFC 9112) line
 folding, permitting a header value such as "Two\r\n Three". This left a
 header injection opportunity for certain proxy chains (CWE-444). The fix
 rejects any header value containing CR or LF outright.
 .
 Note: this patch backports upstream commit 758be0c (Finding 2, obs-fold
 / CRLF header injection). It does NOT address the separate %00 URI
 truncation issue (Finding 1), which has no upstream fix commit.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/libevent/libevent/commit/758be0c0f69c1934ef9a84ab39e9f9e5fde2e6d0
Author: Nick Mathewson <nickm@torproject.org>
Last-Update: 2026-08-22
---
--- a/http.c
+++ b/http.c
@@ -1955,13 +1955,11 @@ evhttp_header_is_valid_value(const char *value)
 {
 	const char *p = value;

-	while ((p = strpbrk(p, "\r\n")) != NULL) {
-		/* we really expect only one new line */
-		p += strspn(p, "\r\n");
-		/* we expect a space or tab for continuation */
-		if (*p != ' ' && *p != '\t')
-			return (0);
+	if (strpbrk(p, "\r\n") != NULL) {
+		/* Reject any header containing CR or LF. */
+		return (0);
 	}
+
 	return (1);
 }

--- a/test/regress_http.c
+++ b/test/regress_http.c
@@ -2406,7 +2406,8 @@ http_bad_header_test(void *ptr)
 	TAILQ_INIT(&headers);

 	tt_want(evhttp_add_header(&headers, "One", "Two") == 0);
-	tt_want(evhttp_add_header(&headers, "One", "Two\r\n Three") == 0);
+	tt_want(evhttp_add_header(&headers, "One", "Two Three") == 0);
+	tt_want(evhttp_add_header(&headers, "One", "Two\r\n Three") == -1);
 	tt_want(evhttp_add_header(&headers, "One\r", "Two") == -1);
 	tt_want(evhttp_add_header(&headers, "One\n", "Two") == -1);
 	tt_want(evhttp_add_header(&headers, "One", "Two\r") == -1);
Description: CVE-2026-63382 - Fix HTTP request smuggling in libevent's evhttp server
 libevent's HTTP layer was vulnerable to request smuggling (GHSA-q39v-w2g7-gr8j).
 Two issues were addressed:
 .
 1. HTTP chunk sizes were parsed with EVBUFFER_EOL_CRLF, which accepts a bare
    LF as a line terminator. RFC 9112 requires chunk lines to be terminated by
    CRLF. Accepting bare LF lets an attacker desynchronise front-end and
    back-end parsers. The chunk-size reader now uses EVBUFFER_EOL_CRLF_STRICT
    so only CRLF terminates a chunk line.
 .
 2. The body framing logic only checked for a single "Transfer-Encoding: chunked"
    header via an exact string compare and did not reject conflicting framing
    headers. This patch adds evhttp_validate_len_and_encoding_(), which rejects
    requests that contain both Transfer-Encoding and Content-Length, duplicate
    Content-Length headers, "chunked" appearing anywhere but as the final
    transfer-coding, or a repeated chunked encoding. Transfer-Encoding parsing
    is tightened to correctly handle comma-separated codings and OWS/parameters
    (evhttp_str_is_chunked_/evhttp_check_transfer_encoding_). The computed
    "chunked" state is stored on the request and consumed by evhttp_get_body().
 .
 This is a backport of the upstream fix to 2.1.12-stable; it applies cleanly
 with no adaptation.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/libevent/libevent/commit/10abb34b8dc3e1184de315dd261ce4b77563cda6
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/libevent/libevent/commit/ac38703b2d312200c4f967f02936af0118d384a0
Bug: https://github.com/libevent/libevent/security/advisories/GHSA-q39v-w2g7-gr8j
Author: libevent developers
Last-Update: 2026-08-22
